  "status": "formal",
  "supportedClaim": "For the stated finite Fourier compressions, the moving complement retains a positive-real conjugate pair after the leading cluster is removed; the three stored vertical-line resolvent peak series and semigroup grid are independently reproduced; and a fixed inviscid projection exhibits severe long-time leakage. These finite findings motivate selecting all top clusters and moving projections, but prove no continuum spectral, resolvent, continuous-time, nonautonomous, nonlinear, or Clay statement.",
